      "text": "Nothing is specified in the law as to the age at which a priest might begin to exercise his office. Levites were qualified according to the law at 30 or 25 (Num. 4:3; 8:23–26), and according to later usage at 20 (1 Chr. 23:24, 27). Consecration to the priestly office consisted of two parts: ceremonial and sacrificial.",
